WEBVTT

00:09.180 --> 00:12.950
<i>Turning now to the attack on McMurdo Base in the Antarctic a few days ago.</i>

00:12.950 --> 00:17.640
<i>While no details have been confirmed as yet, we can partly report that there are some who say...</i>

00:17.640 --> 00:21.990
<i>...that it is related to the enormous air current mass discovered on the Ross Ice Shelf.</i>

00:22.090 --> 00:25.210
<i>In response to the attack, the president said in his address...</i>

00:25.210 --> 00:29.100
<i>...a short while ago that he was prepared to mount "a determined counterattack".</i>

00:29.100 --> 00:33.750
<i>As a result, tensions in many countries in the southern hemisphere have risen precipitously,</i>

00:33.740 --> 00:38.260
<i>...and there are unconfirmed reports that panic-fueled riots have broken out in some areas.</i>

00:38.260 --> 00:41.270
<i>At the moment, communications with those at McMurdo Base...</i>

00:41.290 --> 00:44.740
<i>...have yet to be restored, and authorities fear for their safety.</i>

00:44.740 --> 00:48.580
<i>We're standing by to go live with an interview with the president.</i>

00:48.580 --> 00:50.720
<i>Please wait a moment while we get that ready.</i>

01:02.490 --> 01:05.480
I'm Nagumo, the commander of this mobile fleet.

01:06.060 --> 01:11.760
I'm honored to meet so many members of the press here today.

01:13.470 --> 01:17.230
Why is the Japanese military dispatching such a large fleet at this time?

01:17.440 --> 01:21.050
Is Japan trying to win a permanent seat on the UN Security Council?

01:22.580 --> 01:29.610
Our forces are here merely to fulfill a formal request issued by the United Nations to our government.

01:29.640 --> 01:34.150
This is because defense of the Antarctic is of common interest to all humanity.

01:34.360 --> 01:37.820
Is that supposing an attack by the JAM, sir?

01:38.360 --> 01:41.960
Our duty is to defend the Passageway.

01:42.800 --> 01:48.100
And that applies to any enemies which come through the Passageway from off-world.

01:48.340 --> 01:49.540
You mean...

01:49.540 --> 01:53.700
Any comments on aspirations of becoming a leading nation in the UN forces in the next term?

01:53.700 --> 01:58.190
What do you think of the extreme wariness of that expressed by various Asian nations?

01:59.270 --> 02:02.120
<i>Roger, Uniform November four-zero-one!</i>

02:02.120 --> 02:06.290
<i>Hotel Victor zero-niner, I will go to point three-three for sea patrol.</i>

02:06.290 --> 02:09.260
<i>Hotel Victor zero-niner, Roger.</i>

02:09.260 --> 02:13.630
<i>Bravo Charlie Delta Echo, this is Admiral.</i>

02:13.630 --> 02:17.160
<i>Mike Charlie zero-eight-zero, over.</i>

02:20.070 --> 02:24.140
Thank God... They've finally left.

02:24.140 --> 02:26.510
Maybe things will quiet down a little now...

02:26.510 --> 02:29.080
Oh! Ms. Jackson-san, excuse me!

02:29.080 --> 02:32.150
I'm sorry one of us asked to be left behind here.

02:32.150 --> 02:34.410
Oh, no, please! It's no trouble at all.

02:35.020 --> 02:37.840
It's a good chance for you to see our forces in action.

02:37.850 --> 02:40.550
Right. Believe me, I'll be seeing as much as I can.

02:44.660 --> 02:46.920
That's why I came here, after all.

03:56.750 --> 03:57.650
Sentou Yousei Yukikaze

03:57.880 --> 04:05.270
Battle Fairy

03:57.880 --> 04:05.270
YUKIKAZE

04:09.180 --> 04:14.390
As you are aware, as we introduce our various new technologies and weaponry...

04:14.580 --> 04:18.320
...one by one, they are copied by the JAM.

04:18.350 --> 04:23.320
The battle situation up till now has been a back and forth stalemate.

04:25.190 --> 04:27.650
In regard to our strategic methods up till now,

04:27.660 --> 04:32.170
in the case of the JAM bases confirmed by our strategic reconnaissance corps,

04:32.170 --> 04:37.330
our basic strategy in attacking or bombing them has been as a containment tactic.

04:38.570 --> 04:42.380
In response, the JAM appear from completely different points...

04:42.380 --> 04:44.680
...and raid us from behind.

04:44.680 --> 04:47.180
We've seen this pattern over and over.

04:47.580 --> 04:52.180
According to analysis of the latest observation results by the Central Computer...

04:52.690 --> 04:57.190
...this pair of JAM bases seems to have a prescribed set of rules covering them.

04:57.490 --> 04:58.900
The Antarctic?!

04:59.500 --> 05:02.360
Yes. You and Lt. Fukai, together.

05:02.700 --> 05:05.530
At a time like this?! What now?

05:05.530 --> 05:08.630
The Super Phoenix Mark-11.

05:09.070 --> 05:12.730
A combustion test of the new engine built for B-3.

05:13.210 --> 05:15.540
It's to be conducted in the Earth's atmosphere.

05:34.430 --> 05:37.520
We've contacted them on the Earth side, so don't worry.

05:38.590 --> 05:40.900
I doubt they'll suddenly start shooting at you.

05:42.100 --> 05:43.400
Now then, Colonel.

05:43.770 --> 05:44.930
I'll explain.

05:46.580 --> 05:52.280
The reinforcement armor system developed by the Systems Corps: BAX-4.

05:52.280 --> 05:54.230
We will form a combat unit with it...

05:54.980 --> 06:01.090
...and after the large-scale bombardment of the two strongholds at Richwar and Cookie, we'll send this in.

06:01.090 --> 06:04.670
We will take complete control of the ground at the JAM strongholds.

06:05.170 --> 06:08.660
Now, as far as the vital members of our ground forces...

06:09.230 --> 06:14.560
...we will take the "redundant" members showing up in our forces due to the crash of transport units and so on,

06:14.840 --> 06:17.740
bring them in for nominal "retraining"...

06:17.740 --> 06:23.410
...and form them into a special temporary unit. A list of candidates is being drawn up now.

06:26.850 --> 06:30.790
<i>B-3, this is Boomer. Refueling will be complete soon.</i>

06:30.790 --> 06:32.890
<i>Maintain present speed.</i>

06:32.890 --> 06:33.700
<i>Roger.</i>

06:34.960 --> 06:38.590
<i>Done refueling. Separate probe from the drogue.</i>

06:39.160 --> 06:41.120
<i>Roger. Probe retracting.</i>

06:41.960 --> 06:43.800
<i>Good luck, Boomerang.</i>

06:43.800 --> 06:46.830
<i>Thanks, Milky-1. Good luck.</i>

06:57.750 --> 06:59.770
Boomerang, huh?

07:00.480 --> 07:02.420
You making another one?

07:02.420 --> 07:05.440
Yeah. I got a good feeling about this one.

07:06.660 --> 07:08.290
Some people never learn...

07:08.290 --> 07:11.380
It hits a spot deep inside of me.

07:12.190 --> 07:16.960
I made the perfect one a long time ago. With a single-chip artificial intelligence.

07:17.500 --> 07:19.990
I put an ultra-layer LSI in it.

07:20.440 --> 07:21.730
And did it fail?

07:22.500 --> 07:23.870
How'd you know?

07:23.870 --> 07:25.980
You sound really sad.

07:26.000 --> 07:27.960
Even a little kid could tell.

07:43.330 --> 07:45.380
I ended up with three stitches.

07:47.130 --> 07:52.110
Machines are too rigid to fly naturally.

07:57.240 --> 08:01.980
What do you plan on doing when the war's over?

08:01.980 --> 08:04.280
I haven't thought about it.

08:04.950 --> 08:07.130
What about you, Jack?

08:07.980 --> 08:12.580
Yeah... I'll go home and be a farmer.

08:13.090 --> 08:16.390
I know! I'll take you to my home sometime!

08:16.390 --> 08:19.050
It's all farms there. Nothing else out there.

08:20.360 --> 08:22.630
Gonna fly your boomerangs there, too?

08:23.170 --> 08:26.690
Sure. I'll show you my best one.

08:32.880 --> 08:36.570
Q.N.H. is decreasing quickly. Check.

08:37.050 --> 08:39.530
After six-zero seconds, over I.P.

08:40.120 --> 08:42.450
On course now. Fuel?

08:42.450 --> 08:43.680
One-eight-point-zero.

08:43.690 --> 08:45.120
Warning lights check.

08:45.140 --> 08:45.990
Check normal.

08:45.990 --> 08:46.790
Oxygen?

08:46.790 --> 08:48.260
Oxygen check, okay.

08:48.260 --> 08:49.200
Oil pressure?

08:49.260 --> 08:50.130
Normal.

08:50.150 --> 08:51.590
Exhaust temperature?

08:51.590 --> 08:53.120
Eight hundred. Normal.

08:54.800 --> 08:56.300
Bogies at three o'clock!

08:56.320 --> 08:59.870
Type-2s! Three! They're headed for the Passageway!

08:59.870 --> 09:02.810
Shit... Where the hell are our patrols?!

09:03.340 --> 09:05.770
Rei! Let's shoot them down!

09:05.770 --> 09:07.640
We can't from here!

09:07.640 --> 09:09.310
I'm taking us in!

09:09.310 --> 09:11.750
We're bringing home a hell of a souvenir!

09:13.220 --> 09:15.280
Two-zero seconds before inrush!

09:15.280 --> 09:18.590
Indicated airspeed: 500 knots!

09:18.590 --> 09:21.060
Check! Electrification voltage!

09:21.590 --> 09:25.120
Now, 300 millivolts and increasing.

09:26.460 --> 09:27.780
Gate in sight.

09:28.830 --> 09:30.090
Inrush!

09:39.980 --> 09:42.470
<i>Three units? You sure you're not reading echoes?</i>

09:42.480 --> 09:43.710
<i>No doubt about it.</i>

09:44.350 --> 09:47.840
<i>This isn't what the report said!
They're headed for restricted airspace!</i>

09:47.840 --> 09:49.690
<i>Intercept at once! Eagle-1! Eagle-2!</i>

09:50.190 --> 09:51.490
<i>Eagle-1, roger!</i>

09:51.490 --> 09:52.220
<i>Two, roger!</i>

09:52.890 --> 09:55.060
<i>Hawkeye to Admiral-56.</i>

09:55.060 --> 09:58.030
<i>Variance from report. Reading 3 FAF units.</i>

09:58.030 --> 10:01.550
<i>They're heading for restricted airspace. Eagle moving to intercept.</i>

10:01.860 --> 10:03.570
<i>Admiral, roger and out!</i>

10:04.100 --> 10:06.260
<i>Target, in sight. One o'clock, low.</i>

10:08.540 --> 10:11.710
<i>This is the Japanese Navy, attached to the U.N. Forces.</i>

10:11.710 --> 10:16.260
<i>FAF, you are about to leave your prearranged flight area.</i>

10:20.420 --> 10:22.590
<i>All hands, air raid stations!</i>

10:22.750 --> 10:24.980
<i>All hands, air raid stations!</i>

10:25.390 --> 10:27.750
<i>Eagle and Dragon squadrons, launch at once!</i>

10:27.990 --> 10:30.180
<i>Intercept unidentified aircraft!</i>

10:30.180 --> 10:31.870
<i>All hands, air raid stations!</i>

10:32.290 --> 10:34.350
<i>All hands, air raid stations!</i>

10:34.760 --> 10:37.280
<i>Eagle and Dragon squadrons, launch at once!</i>

10:45.970 --> 10:50.810
<i>FAF unit, disarm at once and follow me!</i>

10:50.810 --> 10:53.890
<i>This is the Japanese Navy, attached to the U.N. Forces.</i>

10:54.350 --> 10:56.540
This is no time to surround us!

10:57.150 --> 10:58.840
The JAM will eat us alive!

10:59.760 --> 11:01.720
<i>Disarm and follow me!</i>

11:01.720 --> 11:07.960
<i>I say again! FAF, this is the Japanese Navy, attached to the United Nations.</i>

11:07.960 --> 11:11.730
<i>You have been intercepted. Disarm and follow me.</i>

11:12.130 --> 11:14.710
Three bogies, closing on our fleet at high speed!

11:14.800 --> 11:16.370
Where are our interceptors?

11:16.370 --> 11:18.230
About 10 minutes to contact, sir!

11:18.540 --> 11:20.480
All ships, fire surface to air missiles!

11:20.480 --> 11:21.900
Surface to air missiles, aye!

11:22.280 --> 11:24.220
<i>All stations, launch SAMs!</i>

11:24.600 --> 11:26.900
<i>All stations, launch SAMs!</i>

11:38.290 --> 11:40.760
The Earth fleet's launched missiles.

11:41.650 --> 11:43.170
The JAM will outmaneuver them.

11:43.170 --> 11:46.370
From that close range, the carrier will be...
This is bad!

11:46.370 --> 11:48.870
Rei! Let's shoot those things down!

11:49.050 --> 11:51.640
Not enough fuel. We won't be able to go back.

11:51.660 --> 11:54.800
That doesn't matter! We have to do what we can!

12:03.690 --> 12:05.390
<i>Wha- What the hell was that...?!</i>

12:05.390 --> 12:06.390
<i>Intercept!</i>

12:06.390 --> 12:07.690
<i>Roger!</i>

12:34.320 --> 12:36.310
<i>Contact lost with Dragon-3!</i>

12:38.450 --> 12:41.020
<i>Dragon-3 and 4, lost!</i>

12:41.020 --> 12:43.070
<i>They're headed for home! After them!</i>

12:57.540 --> 12:58.880
Target closing!

12:58.900 --> 13:01.370
Is it ECM...? What the hell?!

13:15.660 --> 13:18.350
The Earth forces are totally outmatched.

13:20.420 --> 13:21.590
Found them! Over there!

13:25.700 --> 13:27.490
They're going for the carrier!

13:27.670 --> 13:29.490
This is one crazy engine test.

13:48.220 --> 13:49.860
They're coming right for us!

13:49.860 --> 13:51.180
Ram 'em if you have to!

13:51.180 --> 13:52.850
No good! No time!

13:56.900 --> 13:58.870
It exploded...

13:59.590 --> 14:01.730
Another unit, approaching from portside!

14:08.540 --> 14:09.530
JAM...?

14:34.000 --> 14:35.430
Safe, by a hairsbreadth.

14:36.970 --> 14:38.940
That took some years off my life.

14:41.810 --> 14:42.440
Jack.

14:46.520 --> 14:48.750
We're gonna be taking a swim soon.

14:48.750 --> 14:52.910
Relax. If you want fuel, there's plenty.

14:53.390 --> 14:54.580
Down there?

14:55.290 --> 14:59.280
There are international treaties. They can't say no.

15:01.030 --> 15:02.920
Carrier to Eagle-5.

15:02.060 --> 15:04.060
Hawk-2,
we're closed to any landings!

15:03.330 --> 15:04.930
Emergency call!

15:04.930 --> 15:07.110
Abort approach at once!

15:04.930 --> 15:07.110
Fuel? We'll get a tanker
to you ASAP!

15:07.470 --> 15:12.070
Right, the FAF unit is making an emergency landing.
Clear the deck for them.

15:12.070 --> 15:15.370
That's right. We're getting a visit from the space men.

15:25.220 --> 15:27.420
Idiot! He's coming in too high!

15:28.120 --> 15:29.180
Too fast!

15:30.530 --> 15:31.930
Forget it! He's gonna crash!

15:31.930 --> 15:33.050
He won't make it!

15:52.680 --> 15:54.510
Profiling?

15:55.050 --> 15:59.020
You mean, regard the JAM as a single personality?

15:59.020 --> 16:02.580
Yes. I want you to analyze their next move.

16:07.400 --> 16:10.530
Well, I can give you my subjective analysis, but...

16:10.530 --> 16:12.780
Why the sudden rush on this?

16:15.170 --> 16:18.150
No matter how we advance the development of our machines...

16:18.410 --> 16:22.240
...fighting a war without humans is simply impossible.

16:22.840 --> 16:25.380
Well, that's just common sense.

16:27.380 --> 16:29.410
For us, perhaps.

16:31.020 --> 16:38.190
Until now, the JAM have recognized only our machines and computers as their enemies.

16:38.890 --> 16:39.860
But now...

16:39.920 --> 16:44.810
They've changed tactics and are now targeting humans.

16:45.630 --> 16:47.000
Correct.

16:47.000 --> 16:53.830
From drafting battle plans to budget checks, our forces here entrust everything to our computers.

16:54.910 --> 16:59.070
They aim to wring out the uncertain, so-called "human element" from it...

17:01.180 --> 17:04.210
Then the tactical intelligence is already...

17:05.050 --> 17:06.490
No! Surely we wouldn't do that!

17:07.920 --> 17:10.480
You would if you wanted to survive.

17:16.730 --> 17:20.670
No matter what, don't let your guard down, Edith.

17:21.370 --> 17:23.840
We don't have much time. I'm counting on you.

17:25.940 --> 17:27.430
Aunt Rydia...

17:59.210 --> 18:01.440
Some reception, huh?

18:04.750 --> 18:06.300
I'm liaison officer Ishikawa.

18:06.820 --> 18:09.550
The matter of your request for refueling here...

18:09.550 --> 18:13.020
...has been passed to the U.N. and taken up with the FAF.

18:13.020 --> 18:15.980
Once we're clear on the legalities of this, we'll begin work.

18:15.980 --> 18:17.980
We appreciate your consideration.

18:20.830 --> 18:24.200
I'm Major James Bukhar, FAF special forces.

18:24.770 --> 18:27.590
Could you please pass that along to your fleet commander?

18:27.600 --> 18:30.260
Of... Of course, sir! One moment, please!

18:45.550 --> 18:47.820
How long are they gonna just ignore us?

18:51.890 --> 18:55.890
Even saying it couldn't be helped, we've gotten them mixed up in this.

19:01.270 --> 19:04.900
They can't just say "Welcome to Earth!"

19:06.540 --> 19:09.080
It's not like we attacked them.

19:12.200 --> 19:16.550
From their point of view, we might as well have.

19:23.990 --> 19:24.800
Hi there!

19:29.560 --> 19:31.590
What a magnificent plane...

19:34.270 --> 19:35.790
Very lovely.

19:42.180 --> 19:45.200
It's a special model made just for the SAF, right?

19:46.550 --> 19:48.380
The FRX-00.

19:48.380 --> 19:54.380
I believe for formal deployment, it's now designated the FFR-44-MR.

19:57.290 --> 20:01.260
If it weren't for you, this ship would have been in real trouble.

20:01.260 --> 20:03.840
Thank you. I appreciate it.

20:04.570 --> 20:06.260
Pardon me, but...

20:06.260 --> 20:08.870
Oh, my! Forgive me!

20:08.870 --> 20:12.330
I'm Lynn Jackson, a journalist.

20:13.740 --> 20:14.970
Lynn...

20:15.680 --> 20:17.820
Oh! "The Invader!"

20:18.550 --> 20:22.880
I'm honored to find out someone in the FAF has read it.

20:22.880 --> 20:26.450
It's a good book. A significant work.

20:27.260 --> 20:30.550
I'm James Bukhar. And that's...

20:32.490 --> 20:33.610
...Rei Fukai.

20:36.700 --> 20:39.130
He's the pilot of Yukikaze here.

20:39.430 --> 20:41.100
Yukikaze...

20:42.200 --> 20:44.010
It has a wonderful ring to it.

20:44.770 --> 20:46.380
A good name.

20:46.810 --> 20:50.650
It's sort of a nickname for it. You're staying aboard here?

20:50.650 --> 20:52.670
Yes, for my research.

20:52.910 --> 20:55.710
If it's all right, may I talk to you for a bit?

20:59.220 --> 21:03.640
The commander apparently wants to meet with you. I'll show you to his quarters.

21:04.490 --> 21:06.120
Roger that.

21:07.230 --> 21:09.030
Until later, then.

21:15.540 --> 21:18.400
After finally getting back to Earth...

21:22.010 --> 21:25.590
That's how everyone on Earth acts now.

21:27.250 --> 21:30.600
Even though the JAM are so close to us...

21:30.610 --> 21:35.310
They make even the existence of the JAM a tool of war.

21:37.660 --> 21:39.350
It's as though you...

21:41.900 --> 21:43.540
...aren't from Earth anymore.

21:46.070 --> 21:47.710
Perhaps you're right.

21:49.040 --> 21:50.070
And you, too.

21:50.640 --> 21:52.770
It's like you're a space man.

21:54.310 --> 21:57.340
Now that you talk, I see you have an unexpectedly nice voice.

22:22.000 --> 22:24.480
Even I don't really understand it.

22:25.610 --> 22:28.300
Why am I so obsessed with it?

22:30.510 --> 22:34.880
When I was a child, and first saw the news footage of the JAM...

22:35.420 --> 22:37.380
It was so horrible...

22:41.390 --> 22:45.790
I wanted to know what it was that scared me,

22:45.790 --> 22:50.700
so I started studying all sorts of things, and before I realized...

22:50.700 --> 22:53.050
...I'd alienated even my own family.

22:56.840 --> 23:01.980
Even though it was once a "threat to mankind" which panicked everyone...

23:02.680 --> 23:05.610
...it's as though everyone has forgotten about it.

23:07.420 --> 23:11.210
Forgotten that the alien world Fairy is on the other side of the Passageway...

23:11.220 --> 23:14.920
...and that the war there is still going on.

23:22.430 --> 23:25.720
But the JAM are a reality.

23:25.970 --> 23:28.630
A real threat.

23:31.540 --> 23:34.300
To fight such an alien enemy...

23:34.680 --> 23:36.870
...all you can do is rise to face them.

23:37.780 --> 23:41.650
Because there's no place we can ever run from them.

25:09.400 --> 25:12.000
There are things we do that depress me greatly.

25:12.210 --> 25:14.580
I've never seen anything
like that.

25:12.610 --> 25:14.990
But I still have hope.

25:16.740 --> 25:19.470
I still believe humanity isn't as foolish as I fear.

25:21.250 --> 25:24.510
Perhaps for now we don't see what's around us...

25:25.890 --> 25:27.980
...but someday, surely.

25:32.530 --> 25:35.360
Farewell, visitors from Fairy.

25:48.040 --> 25:50.060
Earthmen, huh?

26:07.200 --> 26:09.790
What's going on? Is it the JAM? Wha...?!

26:37.060 --> 26:38.110
It's him.

26:45.400 --> 26:47.750
It's asking for combat maneuvering control?!

27:34.320 --> 27:36.580
<i>All you can do is rise to face them.</i>

27:37.460 --> 27:41.680
<i>Because there's no place we can ever run from them.</i>

28:08.150 --> 28:13.150
In my dreams, it comes so clearly.

28:14.560 --> 28:20.320
Letting me embrace that day.

28:22.730 --> 28:27.600
I've seen a lot of summers off...

28:29.070 --> 28:35.300
...along the way to now.

28:36.640 --> 28:39.240
Long way to home.

28:39.040 --> 28:43.040
Because I love your smile...

28:42.910 --> 28:49.480
...that never changes.

28:51.050 --> 28:53.720
Long way to home.

28:53.590 --> 28:57.550
I'll be going back soon.

28:57.420 --> 29:00.990
I'll walk till dawn...

29:00.860 --> 29:03.960
...back to you.

29:05.630 --> 29:08.730
My sweet home!

29:08.600 --> 29:12.130
I wanna back right now!

29:12.970 --> 29:15.970
My sweet home!

29:15.880 --> 29:19.140
I wanna hold your mind!

29:23.880 --> 29:26.480
Long way to home.

29:26.350 --> 29:30.350
Let's head back right now.

29:30.220 --> 29:36.730
Because I long to see your smile.

29:38.430 --> 29:41.100
Long way to home.

29:40.900 --> 29:44.830
I'll be going back soon.

29:44.700 --> 29:48.440
I'll walk till dawn...

29:48.240 --> 29:52.070
...back to you.

30:24.210 --> 30:28.180
Sentou Yousei Yukikaze

30:30.960 --> 30:34.890
A traitor's work brings the FAF to the brink of disaster.

30:35.500 --> 30:40.170
Within the apocalyptic battle which swallows up everything...

30:40.170 --> 30:43.900
...flies Mave, the queen of the wind.

30:43.900 --> 30:46.770
To finish her personal battle.

30:47.440 --> 30:49.940
Together with Rei Fukai...
